 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to the New York state scenic\nbyways system",
    "basePrintNo": "S3449",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3449-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §349-dd, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3449\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to the New York state\nscenic byways system\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo name and describe various state, county, and local roads in the Towns\nof Durham and Windham in Greene County as the \"Durham Valley Scenic\nByway\",\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one adds a new paragraph j-14 to subdivision 1 of section 349-dd\nOf the highway law, including the Durham Valley Scenic Byway as a compo-\nnent of the New York State Scenic Byways system.\n\nSection two provides for an immediate effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe proposed roadways were designated as scenic roads by the New York\nState Department of Environmental Conservation prior to the creation of\nthe New York State Scenic Byways program by the State Legislature in\n1992 (paragraph k of subdivision 1 of section 349-dd of the Highway\nLaw). However, these roadways have not been specifically identified in\nlaw as such.\n\nThis legislation, following the recommendation of the New York State\nScenic Byway Advisory Board, would name and describe the \"Durham Valley\nScenic Byway\" in a manner similar to other New York State Scenic Byways.\nThis proposal would also link the existing scenic road sections with\nadditional sections to remove all gaps in the route, to create one\ncontinuous scenic byway.\n\nScenic byways provide tremendous benefits to the communities through\nwhich they pass, including increased economic benefits from tourism,\nimproved traveler and community services, more careful environmental\nstewardship of the byway corridor, and the potential to access federal\ngrants to develop the byway.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: 88759 RULES / A10781 transportation\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
